ty seriously.\n\nOverall, B seems strong on reliability and stress, but communication issue is big. D strong on responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but hot temper.\n\nMaybe D is best because strengths cover many criteria: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, adaptability (responds to unexpected), but hot temper is concerning. However, hot temper could be mitigated? Show-off maybe less severe.\n\nWe need to argue. As first speaker, we can propose a candidate and explain. Could also ask for clarification from other panel members about certain concerns. But we have to use tool only if needed. We could ask another panel member about any additional info on candidate D's hot temper severity. But we have to ask via tool before public message if needed. However we can still make an argument now.\n\nGiven no prior discussion, we can state our provisional recommendation. Choose candidate D? Let's weigh: D has strong responsibility, concentration, problem solving, adaptability, but hot temper and know-it-all. B has conscientiousness, stress, but nasty remarks and weak memory. Which is more critical? Nasty remarks may be more severe for crew cooperation than hot temper? Both are serious. But D's hot temper may affect crisis situations. B's nasty remarks may affect daily interactions.\n\nMaybe candidate A? Show-off and not open to new ideas are concerns but maybe less severe than overt hostility. A has strong anticipation, spatial vision, leadership. Could be best overall.\n\nLet's decide: I think candidate A's strengths in anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership are highly relevant for long-distance flights. The negatives (show-off, not open to new ideas) are concerning but perhaps less critical than overt hostility. So I will recommend Candidate A.\n\nWill state that I recommend Candidate A, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and suggest we need to discuss the impact of show-off behavior.\n\nProceed."}
